________________", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1445, "answer": {"text": "D", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 3, "prompt": "Checkpoints and (immunostat function)\nAnswer __________________", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1508, "answer": {"text": "A", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 4, "prompt": ".Didn`t achieve any proper result.\nAnswer __________________", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1578, "answer": {"text": "D", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 5, "prompt": "Talking about the process of removal of cancer cells.\nAnswer __________________", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1644, "answer": {"text": "B", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 8, "prompt": "Did experiments or endeavors with respect to T-cells lead to any significant\nresults or immune responses?\nAnswer _________________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 255, "answer": {"text": "No", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 9, "prompt": "At which stage the nature of the immune response is determined?\nAnswer ___________________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 392, "answer": {"text": "Stage 3", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 10, "prompt": "Which cells may find it difficult to home to tumors?\nAnswer _________________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 488, "answer": {"text": "T cells", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 11, "prompt": "What is the term referred to describe the series of events involved in anticancer\nimmune response?\nAnswer _____________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 574, "answer": {"text": "Cancer-Immunity Cycle", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 12, "prompt": "Presence of what will dampen or disable antitumor immune responses in the\ntumor microenvironment?\nAnswer ______________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 702, "answer": {"text": "immunostat", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 13, "prompt": "What are the most effective approaches in an immunotherapy?\nAnswer _______________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 830, "answer": {"text": "selectively targeting the rate-limiting step", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 14, "prompt": "What target was not achieved so far in immunizing cancer patients?\nAnswer ________________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 921, "answer": {"text": "effective cytotoxic T cell responses", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 15, "prompt": "Destroying the cancer cell releases additional ________________", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 156, "answer": {"text": "tumor-associated antigens", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 16, "prompt": "_____________ is referred to as partial or complete suppression of the\nimmune response of an individual", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 224, "answer": {"text": "immunosuppression", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 17, "prompt": "Majority of the processes with respect to activation of the T-cells comprises use\nof _____________.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 332, "answer": {"text": "therapeutic vaccines", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 18, "prompt": "Presently, the challenge is how to effectively use this understanding and\ndevelop _____________.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 436, "answer": {"text": "new drugs", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 19, "prompt": "In ___________, activated effector T cells may entirely infiltrate the tumor bed.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 537, "answer": {"text": "step 4", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 20, "prompt": "The initial step can provide a response only when it is along with___________,\nwhich can clearly show immunity.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 623, "answer": {"text": "signals", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "68ce521fe5a6266c-p6", "label": "Part B · PART B", "part": "B", "sourceSha256": "68ce521fe5a6266c0dd30f4f72039078b1f54f204bc7f4b4588b5429c743ccde", "pages": [6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13], "questions": [{"number": 1, "prompt": "The GCA symptoms can;\nA. Begin and grow suddenly or gradually.\nB. Begin all of sudden.\nC. Occur more gradually.\nGCA - Giant Cell Arteritis\nThe onset of giant cell arteritis (GCA) may be either abrupt or insidious. GCA may\nbegin with constitutional manifestations such as anorexia, fever, malaise, myalgia,\nnight sweat, and weight loss. These prodromal symptoms may occur for a few days\nand may even stretch out to weeks.\nThe most commonly reported symptoms in patients with GCA are as follows:\n   Headache (initial symptom in 33%, present in 72%)\n   Neck, torso, shoulder, and pelvic girdle pain that is consistent with\npolymyalgia rheumatica (PMR; initial in 25%, present in 58%)\n   Fatigue and malaise (initial in 20%, present in 56%)\n   Jaw claudication (initial in 4%, present in 40%)\n   Fever (initial in 11%, present in 35%)", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 223, "answer": {"text": "B Begin All Of Sudden.", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 3, "prompt": "What this notice talk about?\nA .Patients with LS should undergo a range of ongoing surveillance activities.\nB. Patients with LS are recommended to undergo a range of ongoing\nsurveillance activities.\nC. There are a wide range of ongoing surveillance activities which\nare undertaken by caretakers.\nLS surveillance support initiatives or ideas have included earlier and more frequent\ncolonoscopy, consideration for the transvaginal ultrasound and endometrial\nsampling with the possible recommendation for a total hysterectomy, and clinical\nneurologic examination. Upper endoscopy, annual urinalysis, and pancreatic\ncancer screening may also be considered based on family history. Screening\nguidelines continue to be updated as new research clarifies what recommendations\nare beneficial, but few participants receive repeat genetic counseling to update\nsurveillance and surgical recommendations based on a patient’s specific LS gene\nmutation and family history.", "sourcePage": 8, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "B Patients with LS are recommended to undergo a range of ongoing surveillance", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 5, "prompt": "What is correct?\nA .The average age of PMR patients with amyloidosis is higher than the\naverage age of PMR patients without TA.\nB. the average age of PMR patients without TA (p < 0.0164) is\nsignificantly lower than the average age of PMR patients without amyloidosis.\nC. The average age of PMR patients with TA is significantly higher.\nThe average age of PMR patients\nTotal (female & male)\nFemale\nMale\nPMR versus Ath\n0.4494\n0.2972\n0.4217\nPMR with Ath versus without Ath\n0.4222\n0.2703\n0.0004\nPMR with TA versus without TA\n0.0164", "sourcePage": 10, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "C The average age of PMR patients with TA is significantly higher.", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "68ce521fe5a6266c-p14", "label": "Part C · reading 8.pdf", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "68ce521fe5a6266c0dd30f4f72039078b1f54f204bc7f4b4588b5429c743ccde", "pages": [14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21], "questions": [{"number": 7, "prompt": "Which part of the eye is affected by conjunctivitis?\nA Conjunctiva\nB White membrane\nC Eyelids\nD Only A and B", "sourcePage": 16, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 291, "answer": {"text": "D Only A and B", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 9, "prompt": "What is linked with the herpes infection?\nA Bacterial infections.\nB Viral infections.", "sourcePage": 16, "choices": ["A", "B"], "kind": "question", "offset": 531, "answer": {"text": "B Viral infections.", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 10, "prompt": "What is the most common symptom of conjunctivitis?\nA Mild pain in the eye.\nB Watery eyes.\nC Reddening of the inner and outer eyelid.\nD All of the above.", "sourcePage": 17, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 63, "answer": {"text": "C Reddening of the inner and outer eyelid.", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 14, "prompt": "Which is more common in gonococcal infections?\nA Pain around pelvis.\nB Discharge or pus.\nC Inflammation of the eyes.\nD Reddening of the eyes.\nText 2: Osteomyelitis is an infection of the bone.\nOsteomyelitis is an infection of the bone. Osteomyelitis can occur in infants,\nchildren, and adults. Different types of bacteria typically affect the different age\ngroups: in children, osteomyelitis most commonly occurs at the ends of the long\nbones of the arms and legs, affecting the hips, knees, shoulders, and wrists,\nwhereas in adults, it is more common in the bones of the spine (vertebrae), feet, or\nin the pelvis. There are several different ways to develop the bone infection of\nosteomyelitis. The first is for bacteria to travel through the bloodstream\n(bacteremia) and spread to the bone, causing an infection. This mostly occurs when\nthe patient has an infection elsewhere in the body, such as pneumonia or a urinary\ntract infection that spreads through the blood to the bone. An open wound over a\nbone can lead to osteomyelitis. A recent surgery or injection around a bone can\nalso expose the bone to bacteria and lead to osteomyelitis. Patients with conditions\nor taking medications that weaken their immune system are at a higher risk of\ndeveloping osteomyelitis. Risk factors include cancer, chronic steroid use, sickle\ncell disease, human immunodeficiency virus (HIV), diabetes, hemodialysis,\nintravenous drug users, and the elderly.", "sourcePage": 18, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 52, "answer": {"text": "C Inflammation of the eyes.", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 15, "prompt": "Which of the following statements is not true, according to the information\nprovided in paragraph 1?\nA An osteomyelitis is common among people of all ages.\nB An osteomyelitis can be caused by bacteria.\nC In most of the cases, people who have pneumonia may develop\nosteomyelitis.\nD An osteomyelitis is commonly observed in people who are prone to\nbacterial infections.", "sourcePage": 20, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1205, "answer": {"text": "C In most of the cases, people who have pneumonia may develop", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 16, "prompt": "Which of the following can lead to osteomyelitis?\nA Bacterial infection.", "sourcePage": 20, "choices": ["A"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1597, "answer": {"text": "B An open wound.", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 18, "prompt": "Which type of osteomyelitis is slow in the beginning?\nA Chronic\nB Acute\nC Both chronic and acute\nD None", "sourcePage": 21, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 220, "answer": {"text": "A Chronic", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 19, "prompt": "Which group is more specific for diagnosis?\nA CBC and ESR only\nB Only ESR and CRP\nC CRP, ESR and CBC\nD None", "sourcePage": 21, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 348, "answer": {"text": "D None", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 20, "prompt": "According to paragraph 3, involved bone suggests", "sourcePage": 21, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 480, "answer": {"text": "C Bacterial infected bone", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "68ce521fe5a6266c-p22-extract1", "label": "Part C · A Wounded bone B Operated bone area", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "68ce521fe5a6266c0dd30f4f72039078b1f54f204bc7f4b4588b5429c743ccde", "pages": [22], "ranges": [{"page": 22, "start": 0, "end": 664}], "questions": [{"number": 21, "prompt": "According to paragraph 4, which one of the following statements is not correct?\nA Treatment may be completed within 4 to 8 weeks.\nB The duration of the treatment varies depending on the type of osteomyelitis.\nC Working of the affected area is stopped in order to speed up the treatment.\nD Bone is often replaced with bone graft for perfect treatment.", "sourcePage": 22, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 101, "answer": {"text": "D Bone is often replaced with bone graft for perfect treatment.", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 22, "prompt": "According to paragraph 5, delay in treatment of diagnosis may result in;\nA Inability to walk properly.\nB Permanent damage to bone.\nC Removal of affected bone.\nD None", "sourcePage": 22, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 476, "answer": {"text": "B Permanent damage to bone.", "source": {"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-0859418e5f2b8090ad28", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 8.pdf", "sha256": "0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0859418e5f2b8090ad28f9ae06fa35f52233314ec5ba3e97ee16b5ff92f8df7e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "68ce521fe5a6266c-p22-extract2", "label": "Part C · 22 According to paragraph 5, delay in treatment of diagnosis may result in;", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "68ce521fe5a6266c0dd30f4f72039078b1f54f204bc7f4b4588b5429c743ccde", "pages": [22, 23], "ranges": [{"page": 22, "start": 664, "end": 854}], "questions": [{"number": 22, "prompt": "According to